# What the server needs before Themi starts. Copy to .env next to compose.yml; never commit
# the real file. `deploy/install.sh` (themi install) writes one for you.
#
# Everything else is set on Themi's website, on the Modules page: the Telegram bot, AI
# providers, Google, devices and the rest. A variable from docs/ENVIRONMENT.md set here
# still works, and wins over the website.

# The published image and its version.
THEMI_IMAGE=ghcr.io/madicen/themi
THEMI_VERSION=latest
# The container's memory cap: 700m suits a 1 GB server; 1500m on a 4 GB+ Pi.
# THEMI_MEM_LIMIT=700m

# Themi makes its own secret key on first start (/data/secret.key) and shows it once, to
# save. To bring data from another Themi, set its key here instead:
# THEMI_SECRET_KEY=

# The website's public address (Tailscale Funnel), no trailing slash. The install sets it.
# THEMI_PUBLIC_URL=https://<machine>.<tailnet>.ts.net

# Nightly encrypted backups to S3-compatible storage (Cloudflare R2 or Backblaze B2);
# docs/DEPLOY.md section 7. All four go together.
# THEMI_BACKUP_ENDPOINT=
# THEMI_BACKUP_BUCKET=
# THEMI_BACKUP_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# THEMI_BACKUP_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=

# Updates from the website's Development page (docs/DEPLOY.md, section 9), for the host's
# runner: a fine-grained token with Contents: read-only, to find the newest release.
# THEMI_GITHUB_TOKEN=
# THEMI_REPO=madicen/themi       # only if it isn't the one in THEMI_IMAGE
